{
  "abstract": "This corrected paper replaces the claim that separately SPT-filtered graviton and ghost covariances already yield a nonperturbative unitary gravity theory. It proves a shared-filter BRST chain theorem, a finite-cutoff quantum Ward theorem, a uniform Borel-inheritance theorem, and a conditional cohomological Osterwalder-Schrader reconstruction theorem. Independent filters, TT positivity alone, and permanent Gaussian damping do not supply the missing interfaces. The selected gravitational quantum measure, QME, constructive removal limits, and physical reflection positivity remain explicit exit gates.",
